  "prefLabel": "En 1202.17 Undue delay",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1202.17 \"Undue delay\" means more than 3 business days from the later of the date by which the customer complies with all application requirements or the date for which service was requested, except during severe storms, heavy seasonal activity, and other similar unforeseeable circumstances.\n\nSource. #13986, eff 5-30-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 1200)",
